00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.345
did have to re contextualize
that time because you go,

00:06:32.345 --> 00:06:35.010
we all live in the world
post-Michael Jordan,

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:35.940
post-Air Jordan.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:36.773
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:36.773 --> 00:06:37.606
- You know what I mean?

00:06:37.606 --> 00:06:39.690
So to take us back to that time
right before it all happened

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.800
and what the world looked like.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.533
And it's funny to think
of Nike as an underdog

00:06:42.533 --> 00:06:43.921
'cause they're, so-

00:06:43.921 --> 00:06:44.754
- That's what I'm saying.

00:06:44.754 --> 00:06:45.587
- Everywhere.

00:06:45.587 --> 00:06:46.962
- And then knowing
Adidas, like it was just,

00:06:46.962 --> 00:06:48.060
it was an interesting thing
that I did not know about.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:51.028
Even how I loved when you
and Viola Davis's character

00:06:51.028 --> 00:06:53.190
were at her house and you were just going

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.859
back and forth about like what
to expect in those meetings.

00:06:55.859 --> 00:06:56.692
- Right, right.

00:06:56.692 --> 00:06:57.600
- And they like play it out, like,

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.380
it was brilliant and it was funny,

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.042
but it was really honest as well.

00:07:02.042 --> 00:07:05.280
And it really showed how the
company really got behind him

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:07.380
and y'all literally sank
everything into like,

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.650
they sanked everything
into this one person.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.637
- Well, it seems like a,
like an obvious thing now,

00:07:11.637 --> 00:07:12.717
- [Kelly] But not then.

00:07:12.717 --> 00:07:15.097
- But it was a massive gamble
that they (indistinct).

00:07:15.097 --> 00:07:15.930
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.010
- What I loved about it
is, as you mentioned Viola,

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:17.843
is that you think it's really,

00:07:17.843 --> 00:07:19.770
well, it's gonna be this guy Sunny's Story

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.023
or it's gonna be Michael Jordan's story,

00:07:21.023 --> 00:07:23.490
and you get halfway through the movie,

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.550
which sort of mirrored the
process I had in exploring it

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.950
and trying to put it put together the cast

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.690
and the whole sort of ideas
that were important to me.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:33.630
And you find out really
like, I almost like,

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.169
I was almost embarrassed that it didn't,

00:07:35.169 --> 00:07:36.780
wasn't obviously to begin with.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.795
That without Dolores Jordan, his mother,

00:07:39.795 --> 00:07:40.628
- Yeah.

00:07:40.628 --> 00:07:42.090
- Really guiding him and helping him-

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:42.923
- None of that would've happened.

00:07:42.923 --> 00:07:43.756
- and making us do-

00:07:43.756 --> 00:07:44.589
none of that would happen.
(Chris and Matt murmuring)

00:07:44.589 --> 00:07:45.450
And it just makes so much sense.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.910
Like all these moms, like
I think of my own mom.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.650
My mom loves all my movies,
you know what I mean?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.580
She thinks everything's great.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.683
I'm like, they're not all great mom.

00:07:51.683 --> 00:07:52.516
(everyone laughing)

00:07:52.516 --> 00:07:53.670
But you know, God loves her and your mom,

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.080
nobody loves you like your mother.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.870
And the way that especially young people

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.750
and the case of the NBA and entertainment,

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.670
you see, they get thrust
into these positions,

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.830
sometimes they're from
marginalized communities.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.255
They've historically
been taken advantage of.

00:08:06.255 --> 00:08:07.277
And here they're with these opportunities,

00:08:07.277 --> 00:08:08.110
they're supposed to be negotiating

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.963
with these massive companies.

00:08:09.963 --> 00:08:12.480
It's a whole, you know,

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.130
we know a little bit
about sort of stepping

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.630
from one world into another.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:16.463
It's a lot.

00:08:16.463 --> 00:08:18.630
And if you don't have that
person there to anchor you

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.280
and guide you, you might be in trouble.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.113
- And also though, what you're saying,

00:08:21.113 --> 00:08:22.270
it seems a bit normalized now.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.548
People do fight for
that now, but back then,

00:08:24.548 --> 00:08:26.630
like even on the phone
call, you were like,

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.590
oh ma'am, you don't know how this works-

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.423
- Right.

00:08:29.423 --> 00:08:30.256
- And she was basically like,
but this is how it's going to

00:08:30.256 --> 00:08:31.383
- [Chris, Matt, And Ben] Yeah.

00:08:31.383 --> 00:08:33.374
- if you'd like to work with my-

00:08:33.374 --> 00:08:36.291
and I thought that was so powerful.

00:08:37.143 --> 00:08:38.087
(audience applauding)

00:08:38.087 --> 00:08:38.920
- Because it's important to understand,

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:39.753
the people that said no,

00:08:39.753 --> 00:08:40.723
there's a difference
between a salary and a fee

00:08:40.723 --> 00:08:42.457
and ownership.

00:08:42.457 --> 00:08:43.303
- Yeah.

00:08:43.303 --> 00:08:45.360
- (indistinct) people,
owners, in other words,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.000
you go out and you create
the value in the shoe

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:48.960
by being Michael Jordan.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.940
Well, you are an owner of your identity

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.730
and you should own what
that means to this company.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.140
It's not like, yeah, well
we get to pay your fee

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:55.973
and oh, good for us.

00:08:55.973 --> 00:08:58.410
We make billions of dollars
and you make your fee.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.243
- Yeah.

00:08:59.243 --> 00:09:01.680
I will say one of my favorite parts too,

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.917
and I think that this gets lost sometimes.

00:09:03.917 --> 00:09:05.670
Everybody knows at this point

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.200
Michael Jordan is Michael Jordan.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.520
He is the greatest. Right?

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:09.810
So like, everybody knows that.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.610
So, but the the point is, is that

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.480
everybody doesn't know the
people behind the scenes

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.060
that made that whole brand,

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:16.800
that made all of that
Nike, everything come play.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.646
- By the way, Michael
Jordan's not in the movie.

00:09:17.646 --> 00:09:18.479
- That's powerful. Yeah.

00:09:18.479 --> 00:09:19.312
- On purpose because I-

00:09:19.312 --> 00:09:20.145
- I love that by the way.

00:09:20.145 --> 00:09:21.510
- If you just show somebody,
- You never really see

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:22.530
- you try to pretend-

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:23.363
- Yeah.

00:09:23.363 --> 00:09:24.390
- and tell them this is Michael Jordan,

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.333
because he is so iconic and means so much,

00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:26.166
immediately,
- I thought that was

00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:26.999
brilliant.

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:27.832
- you know, it's a lie.

00:09:27.832 --> 00:09:28.665
Immediately the movie falls apart.

00:09:28.665 --> 00:09:29.673
- Yeah.

00:09:29.673 --> 00:09:30.840
- And what's more interesting
is that the way our heroes,

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.790
these gods kind of operate in our lives

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.860
is not in our day-to-day
lives, but we see them,

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.613
you see him on footage in game films.

00:09:36.613 --> 00:09:37.446
- Yeah.

00:09:37.446 --> 00:09:39.090
- But you know, they're not in real life.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.500
They're larger than life.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:41.333
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:42.166
- And you, the audience
brings their imagination

00:09:42.166 --> 00:09:43.140
and memory to it.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.180
And it's, you know, I do really think

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.770
it's my favorite movie I've ever made.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.880
Viola Davis is amazing.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.359
Julius Tennon--

00:09:49.359 --> 00:09:50.192
- Yeah.

00:09:50.192 --> 00:09:51.025
- I mean Jason Bateman, Chris Tucker.

00:09:51.025 --> 00:09:51.858
- The cast is incredible.

00:09:51.858 --> 00:09:52.691
Yeah.

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:54.326
- These are brilliant,
they did a great job.

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:55.159
I just watched.

00:09:55.159 --> 00:09:55.992
I'm so proud of it.

00:09:55.992 --> 00:09:56.825
It really is fun.

00:09:56.825 --> 00:09:57.658
- [Kelly] The writing is incredible.

00:09:57.658 --> 00:09:58.491
- It really should be seen in the theater.

00:09:58.491 --> 00:09:59.324
It's a lot of fun in the theater.

00:09:59.324 --> 00:10:00.157
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:00.157 --> 00:10:01.440
- April 5th, check it out.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:02.280
- It's so good.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.540
I literally have told everyone.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.575
I literally went to a show,
I did this show last night

00:10:05.575 --> 00:10:09.210
and I walked in and like,
now my eyes go to Jordan's.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.220
And so I'm like, and I
walked in, I was like,

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.598
oh my God you're gonna love the movie.

00:10:12.598 --> 00:10:14.191
I was like, I was, I'm
like you're street team.

00:10:14.191 --> 00:10:16.958
(everyone laughing)

00:10:16.958 --> 00:10:17.791
I'm like, everywhere I go, like literally.

00:10:17.791 --> 00:10:19.110
And then I had conversations
with everybody about this movie

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.440
and I'm like, they're like,
okay, should I see it?

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.331
And I was like, you should 100% see it.

00:10:22.331 --> 00:10:23.164
- [Matt] Yup.

00:10:23.164 --> 00:10:24.109
- I was like, it's so good.

00:10:24.109 --> 00:10:24.942
- This is the beginning of shoe culture.

00:10:24.942 --> 00:10:26.291
- I know.

00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:27.124
- This is the very first time.

00:10:27.124 --> 00:10:27.957
- That's a whole thing too.

00:10:27.957 --> 00:10:30.090
Yeah. It like, it ignited this whole-

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.446
I, my closet is mainly sneakers.

00:10:31.446 --> 00:10:32.481
Like my, like I love it.

00:10:32.481 --> 00:10:33.722
Like I think a lot of us are like that.

00:10:33.722 --> 00:10:35.011
- Mm-hmm. Yup.

00:10:35.011 --> 00:10:36.093
- [Kelly] And boots.

